         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this lesson, we learned that the numbers we use today came from India and that they had different symbols.\n\nThe people of India are not the only ones we thank for these numbers. The Arabs also deserve credit. They chose, among the different ways to write numbers, the one that was most useful to them. That is why we call them **Indo-Arabic**.\n\nHowever, we do not show all numbers on our hands. There are special reasons for this. We will study them in the next lessons.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown/html/text",
               "PostMention": ""
